DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82753\nhttps://forms.gle/dT8tWuDEk4fU65cZA\n\nDescription:\nRegis
 ter for lunch here:\nhttps://forms.gle/dT8tWuDEk4fU65cZA\nDebora Cahn is t
 he creator and showrunner of Netflix’s critically acclaimed drama series
 \nThe Diplomat\n\, starring Keri Russell and Rufus Sewell. Season 4 will p
 remiere on October 15\, 2026. Previous credits include serving as writer a
 nd executive producer on the Showtime series\nHomeland\n\, writer and prod
 ucer of FX’s series\nFosse/Verdon\n\, writer of the HBO film\nPaterno\n\
 , starring Al Pacino\, writer and co-executive producer of Martin Scorsese
 ’s HBO series\nVinyl\n\, writer and producer on ABC's series\nGrey’s A
 natomy\n\, and writer and producer on the landmark NBC drama\nThe West Win
 g\n.\nCahn was nominated for the Emmy Awards\, Critics Choice Awards\, Gol
 den Globes\, Writers Guild and Producers Guild Awards in the Best Drama se
 ries categories for\nThe Diplomat\n. In 2005\, she won the Writers Guild o
 f America Award for Episodic Drama for\nThe West Wing\nepisode "The Suprem
 es."  She won a second Writers Guild of America Award for Best Adapted Lo
 ng Form Television Series for\nFosse/Verdon\n.\n\nSponsor / organizer: Fil
 m & Media Studies Department\n\nAudience: Public\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nW
 hy this was included: Free Food category\; explicit food-service wording\;
  food or meal keyword in title\n\nFood availability is inferred from the s
 ource listing\; verify details before attending.
