DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82250\nhttps://airtable.com/appKrGzSjUnG5V1d3/shr4whdP9BZCDgPb2?p
 refill_I%20am%20registering%20for%3A=Designing%20AI-Resilient%20Assignment
 s&prefill_Ask%20dietary%20question%3F=yes&hide_Ask%20dietary%20question%3F
 =true\n\nDescription:\nAs Generative AI tools continue to proliferate\, fa
 culty are facing the challenge of preserving the integrity of the learning
  process by designing assessments that are resilient to AI use. This half-
 day workshop invites participants to explore practical strategies for crea
 ting assignments and assessments that support learning and avoid AI. We wi
 ll examine a range of AI-resilient assessment approaches\, then consider w
 hich might be most appropriate for participants' specific assignments and 
 courses. Participants will develop their designs with support from facilit
 ators and peers\, drawing inspiration from colleagues’ examples across d
 isciplines.\nLunch will be provided.\nPlease register!\n\nSponsor / organi
 zer: Dartmouth Center for the Advancement of Learning (DCAL)\, Learning De
 sign and Innovation\n\nAudience: Faculty\, Postdoc\, Staff\, Students-Grad
 uate\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was included: explicit food-service 
 wording\; food keyword near service context\n\nFood availability is inferr
 ed from the source listing\; verify details before attending.
