DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://home.dartmouth.edu/events/eve
 nt?event=82771\nhttps://sustainability.stanford.edu/people/kate-maher\nhtt
 ps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfw7zkBdzGQE5K_9DzPzCXSZOIy-ZWLGsiRY
 XL4NVieFeEmIQ/viewform\nhttps://experience.arcgis.com/experience/0a845c134
 d0946649607620ab0b1afe5/#data_s=id:dataSource_39-196cac385a8-layer-9:71\nh
 ttps://irving.dartmouth.edu/research/faculty-seminar-series\n\nDescription
 :\nJoin the Dartmouth Climate Collaborative\, in partnership with the Irvi
 ng Institute for Energy and Society\, for a special faculty seminar.\nSpea
 ker:\nKate Maher\n\, Professor of Earth System Science at Stanford Univers
 ity and Senior Fellow at the Woods Institute for the Environment. Professo
 r Maher's research examines the carbon cycle through multiple lenses\, fro
 m the history of atmospheric carbon dioxide and its impact on the evolutio
 n of life to strategies for sequestering carbon today.\nSpecial guest:\nDr
 . Ansley Booker\, Executive Director of Dartmouth NEXT\, will join to shar
 e more about the university-wide initiative that is expanding opportunitie
 s for students in science\, technology\, engineering\, and mathematics.\nR
 egistration is required\, and seating is limited.\nRegister now\n.\nLunch 
 will be served at 11:45 am. The talk begins at 12 pm\, with time for Q&A a
 t the end.\nMurdough 309 is accessible via the second floor of the Irving 
 Institute.\nSee a campus map\n.\nThe faculty seminar is open to the Dartmo
 uth community of faculty\, staff\, postdocs\, and graduate students.\nThan
 k you to Dartmouth NEXT for their co-sponsorhip of the Faculty Seminar Ser
 ies!\nLearn more about the Faculty Seminar Series\n\nSponsor / organizer: 
 Arthur L. Irving Institute for Energy and Society\n\nAudience: Faculty\, P
 ostdoc\, Staff\, Students-Graduate\n\nSource: Dartmouth\n\nWhy this was in
 cluded: explicit food-service wording\; food keyword near service context\
 n\nFood availability is inferred from the source listing\; verify details 
 before attending.
